{"execute":{"doc":1,"cmd":{"Write":{"PasteMarkdown":{"text":"Project proposal\n\nCommunity repair café for Eastbrook\n\nPrepared for the Eastbrook Neighbourhood Fund · Submitted by Tilly Okonjo · 18 January 2026\n\n# Summary\n\nWe propose a monthly repair café in the Eastbrook Library hall, where volunteers help residents fix clothes, small electricals, bicycles and furniture instead of throwing them away. We ask the Fund for £8,400 to run twelve sessions, train volunteers and buy tools.\n\n# The need\n\nEastbrook households sent an estimated 310 tonnes of bulky and electrical waste to landfill last year. In our survey of 214 residents, 71 % said they had thrown away something that could have been repaired, most often because they did not know how or could not afford a professional repair.\n\n# What we will do\n\n- Run a repair café on the second Saturday of every month, 10 am to 2 pm\n- Recruit and train twenty volunteer fixers, with safety checks for electrical repairs\n- Lend tools between sessions through the library's catalogue\n- Record every repair so that we can report what was saved\n\n# Timeline\n\n| Phase | Months | Milestone |\n|---|---|---|\n| Set-up | February – March | Volunteers recruited, tools bought, insurance in place |\n| Launch | April | First repair café and open day |\n| Running | May – January | Monthly sessions, tool library open |\n| Review | February 2027 | Report to the Fund and the community |\n\n# Budget\n\n| Item | Cost |\n|---|---|\n| Tools and consumables | £3,200 |\n| Volunteer training and safety testing | £1,900 |\n| Hall hire (12 sessions) | £1,440 |\n| Publicity and printing | £860 |\n| Insurance | £1,000 |\n| Total requested | £8,400 |\n\n# Measuring success\n\nBy the end of the first year we aim to repair 600 items, divert at least four tonnes from landfill and have 150 residents attend more than one session.\n"}}}}}
